  "drivers": "The S&P 500 is up about 0.85% near 7,840 after setting a new all-time high, and the Nasdaq Composite is also at a record, as the 10-year yield eases to about 5.26% from Monday's 2002-era peak and WTI slips 1.3% to near $88. Power and nuclear stocks are extending gains after Constellation Energy's 20-year, 890 MW nuclear supply deal with Google (CEG +13.8%, with TLN, VST, LEU, NRG and EROC up 7–14%). AI networking and chips are firm (MRVL +6.6% after raising long-term targets, CIEN +10%, AVGO and AMD near +4%), and NVDA is closing in on a $6 trillion market cap. Biotech has cut its loss (XBI −1.8% vs −3.5% earlier), but genomics and tools names are down 7–12% with no news found, and small caps are flat. August's trade deficit widened to $105.6B; FOMC minutes are due Wednesday.",
